                  <span>Snap <em>store</em></span>
                </a>
              </div>
              <div class="dl-alt" data-os="mac">One app for Apple&nbsp;Silicon and Intel Macs, macOS 10.15 or later</div>
              <div class="dl-alt" data-os="win">Prefer an MSI? <a href={`${DL}/${ALT.msi}`}>Download the .msi installer</a></div>

              <!-- macOS: two ways to install, side by side. Homebrew first, since it
                   avoids the first-launch prompt; the .dmg card explains that prompt. -->
              <div class="dl-alt mac-ways" data-os="mac">
                <section class="way" id="macos-homebrew" aria-labelledby="brew-title">
                  <div class="way-head">
                    <h3 id="brew-title">Install with Homebrew</h3>
                    <span class="way-tag">Recommended</span>
                  </div>
                  <p>No security prompt, and <code>brew upgrade</code> keeps Sarala up to date.</p>
                  <div class="cmd">
                    <div class="cmd-bar"><span>Terminal</span><button type="button" class="gk-copy copy-btn" data-copy="#brew-cmd"><span class="gk-copy-label">Copy</span></button></div>
                    <pre id="brew-cmd">{BREW_CMDS.map((cmd) => <code class="ln">{cmd}</code>)}</pre>
                  </div>
                </section>

                <section class="way" id="macos-first-launch" aria-labelledby="gk-title">
                  <div class="way-head">
                    <h3 id="gk-title">Opening the .dmg the first time</h3>
                  </div>
                  <p>Sarala isn't notarized by Apple (that needs a paid developer account), so macOS asks you to confirm once.</p>
                  <ol class="way-steps">
                    <li><span>Drag <b>Sarala</b> into <b>Applications</b> and open it.</span></li>
                    <li><span>If macOS blocks it, open <b>System Settings › Privacy &amp; Security</b>.</span></li>
                    <li><span>Scroll down and click <b>Open Anyway</b>, then confirm.</span></li>
                  </ol>
                  <details class="way-more">
                    <summary>Prefer Terminal? Use one command instead</summary>
                    <div class="cmd">
                      <div class="cmd-bar"><span>Terminal</span><button type="button" class="gk-copy copy-btn" data-copy="#gk-cmd"><span class="gk-copy-label">Copy</span></button></div>
                    <pre id="gk-cmd"><code>{QUARANTINE_CMD}</code></pre>
                    </div>
                    <p class="fine">This removes the "downloaded from the internet" flag from Sarala only.</p>
                  </details>
                  <p class="fine">On macOS 14 or older, right-click Sarala and choose <b>Open</b> instead. A message saying Sarala "is damaged" is the same warning on Apple Silicon; these steps clear it. You can also <a href={RELEASES} target="_blank" rel="noopener">verify the checksums</a> or <a href={GITHUB} target="_blank" rel="noopener">build it yourself</a>.</p>
                </section>
                <p class="gk-copy-status visually-hidden" id="gk-copy-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <a class="dl-all" href={RELEASES} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                  All releases &amp; checksums
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path></svg>
                </a>
              </div>
            </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ FAQ ============ -->
    <section class="section alt" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="sec-head center reveal">
          <span class="kicker">FAQ</span>
          <h2 id="faq-title">Questions, answered</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="faq reveal">
          {FAQ.map((f) => (
            <details>
              <summary>{f.q}<Fragment set:html={svg("plus")} /></summary>
              <div class="answer">{f.a.map((p) => <p>{p}</p>)}</div>
            </details>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

